                    {
                        "form_id": "b030325d-d59f-49d6-b173-e400d1bcfdb2",
                        "entry_id": "34d43f96-31b4-3c30-ad80-877aa4df533f",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "singular"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Weltliteratur"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8d111dc8-9442-3416-87db-a836c6abd89f",
                        "entry_id": "34d43f96-31b4-3c30-ad80-877aa4df533f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Literatur, die Weltbedeutung hat"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b955ed44-ea16-4fce-bd7b-272c2e68f5a7",
                                "sense_id": "8d111dc8-9442-3416-87db-a836c6abd89f",
                                "text": "Man kann sich darüber streiten, was Weltliteratur ist und was nicht."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "29b34a9d-49a8-46ab-9076-44be6f088238",
                                "sense_id": "8d111dc8-9442-3416-87db-a836c6abd89f",
                                "text": "„Durch die Übernahme des Arthurstoffs auf dem europäischen Festland gingen die Arthurerzählungen in die Weltliteratur ein.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d684a0ba-db57-44aa-a196-291ce6e9b1ff",
                                "sense_id": "8d111dc8-9442-3416-87db-a836c6abd89f",
                                "text": "„Es war ein kräftezehrender Schritt auf die Bühne der Weltliteratur.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd9c3377-65ae-4ed1-b474-edf7e4922418",
                                "sense_id": "8d111dc8-9442-3416-87db-a836c6abd89f",
                                "text": "„Scholem Jankev Abramovitsch (1835-1917) ist der älteste der drei Autoren, die das Jiddische in die Weltliteratur eingeschrieben haben.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f1dec57-05e8-4826-90b2-cc62441b3145",
                                "sense_id": "8d111dc8-9442-3416-87db-a836c6abd89f",
                                "text": "„Wenige Werke der Weltliteratur haben ein so eigenartiges Schicksal erfahren wie die Memoiren des berühmten Venetianers, und selten ist das Bild, das die Nachwelt von dem Autor gewonnen hat, in solchem Maße von dem Geschick des Werkes bestimmt worden.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a0b2a798-1d78-4410-a717-c13f8f4c3f70",
                        "source_entry_id": "34d43f96-31b4-3c30-ad80-877aa4df533f",
                        "source_sense_id": "8d111dc8-9442-3416-87db-a836c6abd89f",
                        "source_sense_description": "Literatur, die Weltbedeutung hat",
                        "target_lang_word": "world literature",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "world literature",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cabeb906-9eea-3074-ba15-67aecb7f44d5",
                                        "entry_id": "a35fdb14-8004-3f06-8fcd-a2b48e78cc7f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Comparative literature."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6e18e9b-1340-345c-8830-a9b56024a9c7",
                                        "entry_id": "a35fdb14-8004-3f06-8fcd-a2b48e78cc7f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The world's national literature collectively, especially the circulation and appreciation of works beyond their country of origin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncommon",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1969236b-425c-4acf-95ff-d277f2084592",
                                                "sense_id": "a6e18e9b-1340-345c-8830-a9b56024a9c7",
                                                "text": "Goethe's notion of world literature, therefore, is linked in an important way to the internationalization of culture that resulted from the emergence of capitalism as the dominant mode of production in modern Europe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "758b1a47-436d-4806-a67f-218c5c1427bd",
                                                "sense_id": "a6e18e9b-1340-345c-8830-a9b56024a9c7",
                                                "text": "In 1827, fresh from his reading of a Chinese novel, Goethe pronounced to Eckermann that \"national literature is now a rather unmeaning term; the epoch of world literature is at hand, and everyone must strive to hasten its approach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca6ebdf3-3c25-41eb-bb05-f8ead188bffa",
                                                "sense_id": "a6e18e9b-1340-345c-8830-a9b56024a9c7",
                                                "text": "If cosmopolitanism and world literature are so closely related, to the point where one may wonder whether “cosmopolitan literature” is synonymous with “world literature” […] a question that needs to be answered is why the concept of cosmopolitanism plays such a minor role in world literature discussions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5f072623-8319-423b-9c47-5ea5dede95d3",
                        "source_entry_id": "34d43f96-31b4-3c30-ad80-877aa4df533f",
